WEBVTT

00:00:07.083 --> 00:00:11.125
You think to press the red button?
Yeah... yes., that's right.

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.833
(Paddington) 'Dear Aunt Lucy.

00:00:13.708 --> 00:00:17.875
'I hope you're still enjoying life
at the Home for Retired Bears.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.333
'It seems a long time since our holiday
together in the valley,

00:00:21.458 --> 00:00:24.083
'and everyone's lives
have changed so much.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.416
'And it was nice of the church
to forgive Clarissa Cabot,

00:00:29.541 --> 00:00:31.750
'providing she became a real nun...'

00:00:31.875 --> 00:00:34.375
- Out.
- Are you sure this is the place?

00:00:35.833 --> 00:00:38.416
(Paddington) '...and took a new posting.'

00:00:39.708 --> 00:00:42.666
(Wailing)

00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:45.791
'Hunter and Gina
have a new boat,

00:00:45.916 --> 00:00:49.500
'thanks to Mr Brown
sorting the insurance for them.

00:00:56.625 --> 00:00:59.958
'As for the Browns,
Jonathan has given up chillin',

00:01:00.083 --> 00:01:02.041
'and is hardly ever in his room.

00:01:02.166 --> 00:01:08.041
'He spends most of his time at trade fairs
doing something he calls hustlin'.

00:01:08.166 --> 00:01:09.750
'The G is silent.'

00:01:09.875 --> 00:01:12.083
The first day of our extremely
dangerous mission...

00:01:12.208 --> 00:01:14.250
(Paddington) 'Mr Brown
has been promoted at work,

00:01:14.375 --> 00:01:17.666
'and he is now Head of Calculated Risk.'

00:01:17.791 --> 00:01:22.166
...finally, with the purple-kneed tarantula
on my face.

00:01:22.833 --> 00:01:26.416
So, as you can see,
some risks are worth embracing.

00:01:26.541 --> 00:01:30.958
But only if they're for the greater good,
and for the people you love.

00:01:32.208 --> 00:01:34.416
- Thank you.
- Outstanding.

00:01:34.541 --> 00:01:36.500
- Sensational.
- Awesome.

00:01:36.625 --> 00:01:40.541
On that note, I will be doing
a sponsored BASE jump

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:43.041
for the Home for Retired Bears.

00:01:43.166 --> 00:01:46.166
So, please chip in.

00:01:46.291 --> 00:01:48.958
And remember, embrace the risk!

00:01:50.708 --> 00:01:55.208
(Paddington) 'Mrs Brown started
a new art project called "Taking Flight".

00:02:00.625 --> 00:02:06.125
'And despite her previous fears,
she's actually closer to Judy than ever.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.750
'Judy's travelogue helped her
get into university,

00:02:08.875 --> 00:02:12.708
'where she's already very busy
at the student newspaper.'

00:02:12.833 --> 00:02:15.875
With a few changes,
this could make the front page.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.583
Thank you.

00:02:17.708 --> 00:02:19.708
Wait... changes?

00:02:22.125 --> 00:02:24.500
(Paddington) 'I hope Mrs Bird
is enjoying her stay with you,

00:02:24.625 --> 00:02:28.583
'and that she's ticked a few things
off her new to-do list.'

00:02:29.875 --> 00:02:32.458
(♪ Jungle music playing)

00:02:35.666 --> 00:02:39.500
The jungle is massive!

00:02:39.625 --> 00:02:41.208
(Groans)

00:02:46.375 --> 00:02:48.041
(Paddington) 'As for me...

00:02:49.333 --> 00:02:52.250
'...I think I made the right decision.

00:02:58.833 --> 00:03:01.666
'Mr Gruber was right when he said
you can have mixed feelings

00:03:01.791 --> 00:03:03.625
'about where you're from.

00:03:04.708 --> 00:03:06.791
'But maybe that's okay.

00:03:07.708 --> 00:03:11.000
'Because I suppose
I am a bit of a mix.

00:03:11.125 --> 00:03:14.791
'Part London, part Peru.

00:03:16.291 --> 00:03:18.708
'A sprinkle of El Dorado.

00:03:22.416 --> 00:03:24.416
'But most of all...

00:03:27.583 --> 00:03:30.083
'...a whole lot of Brown.'

00:03:32.666 --> 00:03:34.916
(Mrs Brown) Paddington, they're here!

00:03:35.041 --> 00:03:39.208
(Paddington) 'Oh, must go.
My guests have arrived for their holiday.'

00:03:39.333 --> 00:03:40.791
- (Footsteps)
- Hello, there!

00:03:40.916 --> 00:03:43.666
- (Pot smashing)
- (Mr Brown) That was my mother's!

00:03:44.875 --> 00:03:47.125
Oh, you've grown.

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:50.458
Come on, let's go and see London!

00:03:58.291 --> 00:04:00.041
Oh, careful!

00:04:00.166 --> 00:04:02.833
(Paddington) Sorry, Mr Brown!

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:08.291
'Love from Paddington.

00:04:08.416 --> 00:04:11.083
'Also known as... (Roaring)

00:04:11.916 --> 00:04:13.750
'...Brown.'

00:04:23.333 --> 00:04:25.541
Look, over there!

00:04:25.666 --> 00:04:26.666
And there!

00:04:26.791 --> 00:04:29.166
Hello! Good morning!

00:04:29.291 --> 00:04:33.750
(♪ "Paddington in Peru" playing
with Peruvian music arrangement)

